Z||000000||formula2||09-16-2001||10:41 PM||||Today I went for a 90 minutes ride.Everything is fine until I exit the highway.I cant shift at all. I let it go on the side of the road for a few seconds ..then it comes to normal ..Like nothing happened..<BR>Same thing on my way back..<P>Looks like my car dont like highways......||||reg||5
Z||000001||afRaceR||09-16-2001||10:53 PM||||My car did the same thing right after I changed the Master and Slave Cylinder. Couldn't understand it. Bleed it, it worked great until I drove it around awhile. Bled it again, and it would be ok.<P>The Only thing I could think of was the NAPA slave cylinder was heating up too much and pretty much boiling the brake fluid. Or maybe it had a small leak in it. I don't think so because it didn't lose fluid, it would actually raise.<P>I put the old GM cylinder back on and it worked fine, except for the leak at the bleeder screw.<P>My advice, go get a GM slave cylinder from GM Parts Direct. Its actually the cheapest place I have found.||||reg||1
